From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:41:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] ath11k: pass an offloaded key exchange to mac80211

The NSS firmware delivers a received data frame on the virtual device's
network device, past mac80211, and that includes the EAPOL frames of the
key exchange. A supplicant that takes the control port mac80211 offers
over nl80211 then never sees them, and an EAPOL frame on the network
device reaches a bridge and anything else listening there, from a station
mac80211 has not checked.

Hand an EAPOL frame the firmware delivers to the receive path the host
uses for a frame the hardware did not decapsulate. It turns the frame back
into 802.11 as it already does for the host's own EAPOL frames, so
mac80211 checks the sender and the port and delivers it over the control
port. The firmware reports no transmit status, so the control port's
transmit status capability is withdrawn while the offload is on.

Rebase this NSS integration onto the shared mac80211/ath11k patch
series while preserving the local host-path fixes.

Refresh against NSS VDEV registration error propagation.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -2726,17 +2726,27 @@ void ath11k_dp_rx_from_nss(struct ath11k
 /* The NSS firmware hands up a frame the hardware did not decapsulate, such
  * as a block ack request, on the same path as ethernet. It goes to mac80211
  * as on the host's own receive path.
+ *
+ * So does the key exchange, which the firmware hands up decapsulated: the
+ * receive path turns it back into 802.11, as it does on the host's own path,
+ * so mac80211 checks the sender and the port and hands it to a supplicant
+ * over the control port rather than to the network device.
  */
 bool ath11k_dp_rx_nss_80211(void *priv, struct net_device *dev,
 			    struct sk_buff *msdu, struct napi_struct *napi)
 {
 	struct hal_rx_desc *desc = (struct hal_rx_desc *)msdu->head;
+	struct ethhdr *ehdr = (struct ethhdr *)msdu->data;
 	struct ieee80211_vif *vif;
 
 	switch (ath11k_dp_rx_h_msdu_start_decap_type(priv, desc)) {
 	case DP_RX_DECAP_TYPE_RAW:
 	case DP_RX_DECAP_TYPE_NATIVE_WIFI:
 		break;
+	case DP_RX_DECAP_TYPE_ETHERNET2_DIX:
+		if (ehdr->h_proto == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE))
+			break;
+		return false;
 	default:
 		return false;
 	}
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -11031,6 +11031,18 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct
 	    ab->hw_params.bios_sar_capa)
 		ar->hw->wiphy->sar_capa = ab->hw_params.bios_sar_capa;
 
+	/* The firmware returns a transmitted frame without saying whether it
+	 * was acknowledged, so a status is not something this driver can
+	 * report. Withdrawn before registration, because the capability is
+	 * read off the wiphy once it is published.
+	 */
+	if (ab->nss_offload) {
+		enum nl80211_ext_feature_index ft =
+			NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CONTROL_PORT_OVER_NL80211_TX_STATUS;
+
+		ar->hw->wiphy->ext_features[ft / 8] &= ~BIT(ft % 8);
+	}
+
 	ret = ieee80211_register_hw(ar->hw);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_err(ar->ab, "ieee80211 registration failed: %d\n", ret);
